tickets.what_to_build:
The first deliverable is conformance cells for the quit sequence. They cite the v44.4.5 app.md before-quit, will-quit and window-all-closed sentences and the browser.cc v44.4.5 state machine (FACT):
- a close veto during quit cancels it;
- window-all-closed is suppressed while quitting;
- a will-quit veto clears quitting;
- a second app.quit() re-emits before-quit.

The facade runs Electron's quit state machine (PANEL-D23 option A, INFERENCE). Facade-initiated app.quit() emits before-quit locally and needs no host→app quit-requested event. Host- or OS-initiated quit sources with no menu dispatch (Dock Quit) arrive as one quit-requested event. INFERENCE: Cmd+Q is the key equivalent of the installed menu's role-quit item, so it reaches this path through F06-T16, not directly. The host enters a pre-Quitting state before the first window closes, so LastWindowClosed during quit is suppressed. This is a normative amendment to KEL-96 §4.5 step 1. After a will-quit veto the host stays alive with zero windows. The AppKit mechanism (terminate cancel plus re-driven Quit, versus delayed reply) is chosen by PANEL-D23's two-arm harness.

Adjacent atoms owned elsewhere:
- per-window close protocol: F02-T3;
- menu roles: role close: F06-T4 (first-proof, through the F02-T3 close path); role quit, including Cmd+Q dispatched through the installed menu's role-quit item: F06-T16 (consumes F01-T3's quit-requested path and flips the F06-T1 role-quit cell, whose implementing ticket is F06-T16);
- quitAndInstall inversion: F09 per PANEL-D23;
- app.exit: F01-T7.

This is not first-proof: the scored workflow ends at a single-window close, which the landed window-all-closed cell already covers. The proof report must record 'Cmd+Q or menu Quit with a dirty window: not scored, unknown'. INFERENCE: until F06-T16 lands, menu Quit and Cmd+Q record F06-T4's KELD-COMPAT diagnostic and do not quit. Until this ticket lands, Dock Quit with an unsaved draw.io document can reach a native terminate with no veto, so the unsaved edit can be lost. That risk is outside the scored cells and is stated, not hidden.

